---
import { company } from '../../data/company';
---

<section class="reading-section" id="problem">
  <div class="content-column">
    <p class="section-code">What we do / 002</p><h2>
      Research time is being spent on everything around the research.
    </h2><p class="lead-copy">
      Environments, disconnected tools, citations, repositories, and lost
      context slow discovery before the real work can begin.
    </p><p>
      Kalaris Labs is building an agent-powered infrastructure layer to take on
      that repetitive technical work while keeping the researcher in control of
      the questions, experiments, and conclusions.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reading-section" id="system">
  <div class="content-column">
    <p class="section-code">The system / 003</p><h2>
      Infrastructure that improves with the work.
    </h2><p class="lead-copy">
      The premise is recursive self-improvement: learn from workflows,
      repositories, papers, and each iteration—then carry that context into the
      next cycle.
    </p><div class="principle-list">
      {
        company.principles.map((principle) => (
          <article>
            <>
              <span>{principle.number}</span>
              <div>
                <>
                  <h3>{principle.title}</h3>
                  <p>{principle.body}</p>
                </>
              </div>
            </>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reading-section" id="culture">
  <div class="content-column">
    <p class="section-code">Culture / 004</p><blockquote>
      “We are societal delinquents. Not because we break laws, but because we
      break expectations.”
    </blockquote><p>
      We are a small, high-agency team. We share what we learn, pursue strange
      questions, and measure the work by lives impacted—not performative
      busyness.
    </p><a class="text-link" href="/team">Read how we work ↗</a>
  </div>
</section>
